# Image → LLM context (vision via Codex CLI)

The model is routed through a text-only proxy: images attached or read with the
Read tool **never reach the model**. Never claim to see an image directly.

To turn an image into usable context (describe, summarize, "use as reference",
OCR, analyze a debug screenshot), delegate to the local `codex` CLI (vision
model, auth via the ChatGPT subscription) and only retrieve the **final text** —
the text passes through the proxy.

## Pre-check

Verify that `codex` is available first:

```bash
command -v codex
```

Missing or logged out (`codex login`) → **STOP** and say so. Never substitute
another vision API and never invent the image content.

## Command

Windows → **Git Bash**, not WSL (WSL bash cannot launch the Windows `codex`, no
`node`). Write the output **outside the workspace** (system temp), so it never
pollutes any repo the rule is ported into:

```bash
& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -lc 'printf "%s" "<INSTRUCTION>" | codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --sandbox read-only --config mcp_servers="{}" -o "$TMP/codex-ctx.txt" -i "/c/absolute/path/image.png" -'
```

From a bash shell directly:

```bash
printf '%s' '<INSTRUCTION>' | codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --sandbox read-only --config mcp_servers='{}' -o "$TMP/codex-ctx.txt" -i "/c/abs/image.png" -
```

Then read the file with the Read tool (Windows path, e.g.
`C:\Users\<user>\AppData\Local\Temp\codex-ctx.txt`) to retrieve the context.

## Rules

- Multiple images: repeat `-i "/c/abs/img.png"` for each one, in a single call.
- `-o <file>` isolates the final message (clean, proxy-safe output). Write it
  outside the workspace (`$TMP/codex-ctx.txt`) then read it back with Read.
  Otherwise, read the last message printed on stdout.
- `--config mcp_servers="{}"` disables `codex` MCP servers and avoids the noisy
  `ERROR rmcp::transport::worker ... connection timeout` lines on stderr. If
  they show up anyway, ignore them: no impact on the result.
- Prompt passed on **stdin** with a trailing `-` (avoids quoting pitfalls).
  Wrap `<INSTRUCTION>` in single quotes; do not pass it as a positional argument.
- Image paths must be **absolute**, in Git Bash style (`/c/Users/...`).
- Never use `OPENAI_API_KEY`; this path goes through the ChatGPT subscription.
- Expect ~30–60 s per call (vision model, several thousand tokens).

## Instructions by intent (`<INSTRUCTION>`)

| Intent | Instruction |
| --- | --- |
| Generic | `Describe this image factually and structured so another LLM can use it as context: subject, layout, colors, verbatim text, style. Be concise.` |
| Character / art ref | `Describe this character reference: silhouette, hair, outfit (pieces/colors/materials), accessories/weapon, palette, pose, render style.` |
| UI / mockup | `Describe this UI: regions, components, verbatim labels, color/spacing cues, interaction hints.` |
| OCR | `Extract ALL text verbatim, preserving reading order. Output only text.` |
| Debug screenshot | `Describe this editor/app screenshot: screen, panels, verbatim error/log text, selected elements, current state.` |
